    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build succeeds. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change: optional owner `postcode` with region-based validation\n\nThe app is Spring PetClinic REST; owners are created via `POST /api/owners`. I added a `postcode` field end-to-end following the existing patterns.\n\n**Files changed:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `postcode` property to the `OwnerFields` schema (type string, `pattern: ^[0-9]{4}$`). Because `Owner` composes `OwnerFields`, this flows into both `OwnerFieldsDto` (input) and `OwnerDto` (output), and MapStruct auto-maps it \u2014 so it's stored and returned. The `@Pattern` also rejects a malformed 4-digit value with a 400 out of the box (null passes, keeping it optional).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `postcode` field (`@Column(name = \"postcode\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n3. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added a `postcode` column to the `owners` table. Tests run under the `hsqldb` profile with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column had to exist in `schema.sql`.\n\n4. **`src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 added `validatePostcode(postcode, city)`, called from `prepareNewOwner`. When present it requires exactly 4 digits and, if the city has a known region (`Owner.regionForCity`), enforces the fixed range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099), throwing `InvalidFieldsException` \u2192 400 otherwise. A city with no known region accepts any 4-digit postcode. A null postcode returns immediately (backward-compatible).\n\n**Note:** the region\u2192range table uses `Map.of`, which rejects a null key \u2014 an unknown city's region is null \u2014 so I guard `region == null` before the lookup (caught by the test run and fixed).\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest` cases \u2014 stores a valid postcode, accepts an owner without one, and rejects a malformed one with 400 \u2014 and the full suite are green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 3/3 passing).",
